# What `eas build` uploads (the mobile app, apps/mobile, #2979).
#
# EAS archives the project from the git root, so without this file every build
# shipped the whole repository: the web app, e2e, docs and a depth-1 `.git` of
# all of it (62 MB, of which apps/mobile is 1 MB). Only apps/mobile is built.
#
# Before you change it:
# - This file REPLACES every .gitignore for the upload, the nested ones too
#   (eas-cli src/vcs/local.ts). Whatever must not leave the machine has to be
#   listed here again: the rules of apps/mobile/.gitignore and the root rules
#   that can match inside apps/mobile are repeated below. Add new ones to both.
# - Only `node_modules` is always left out. `.git` goes too, through the first
#   rule: the build server reads git only for builds it clones itself.
# - No trailing slash on a directory pattern: eas-cli tests a directory as
#   `apps`, not `apps/`, so `!/apps/` would never put it back, and `.expo/`
#   leaves out what is inside but still uploads the empty folder.
# - Check what goes up (apps/mobile/README.md § Building):
#   cd apps/mobile && npx eas-cli@latest build:inspect -p android -e staging -s archive -o <empty dir>

# Everything at the root except apps/, and in apps/ everything except mobile/.
/*
!/apps
/apps/*
!/apps/mobile

# --- apps/mobile/.gitignore, repeated (directories without the slash) ---
node_modules
.expo
dist
web-build
expo-env.d.ts
.kotlin
*.orig.*
*.jks
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision
.metro-health-check*
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*
.DS_Store
*.pem
.env*.local
*.tsbuildinfo
/apps/mobile/android
/apps/mobile/ios
# Firebase / FCM config: EAS gets it from the file env var GOOGLE_SERVICES_JSON.
google-services.json
GoogleService-Info.plist

# --- root .gitignore rules that can match inside apps/mobile ---
.env
.env.*
*.log
*.keystore
coverage
.cache
*.tgz
*.sql.gz
*.[cC][sS][vV]
*.[tT][sS][vV]
*.[xX][lL][sS]
*.[xX][lL][sS][xX]
*.[oO][dD][sS]
.HANDOFF-*
